00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:50.320
So BigQuery is Google Cloud
platform's enterprise data

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.340
warehouse.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.760
It's where big data comes
and lives and thrives.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.130
It goes super fast over
super big amounts of data.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:01.660
It also goes really fast
over smaller amounts of data.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.710
So Firebase is an analyst from
folks working over gigabytes

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:08.350
to fix folks working
over petabytes, works

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.270
equally well for both use cases.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.380
Couple of details here.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.550
It's server-less, which
means you don't have to worry

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.590
about provisioning resources.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.290
You just pipe your data in
and bring your workloads,

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.342
write your queries,
and go for it.

00:03:22.342 --> 00:03:23.800
So you don't have
to spin up nodes.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.610
We take care of all of that
in the background for you.

