00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:34.810
this is a great thing to
do for demonstrations.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:37.202
I don't recommend selecting
all the columns, right?

00:12:37.202 --> 00:12:38.410
BigQuery is a columnar store.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.730
Just pick the ones you want.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:42.850
Because select star
queries can get expensive.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:47.320
So not a best practice, just
an example for the talk.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.510
And so when you
run this query, you

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.580
can see that we've got
an event right here.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.170
And then I'll show you how
that nested and repeated field,

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:54.670
right?

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:58.930
And so here is the
country, the device.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:03.660
And all the way out here you can
start to see that in this row

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:06.290
there are a bunch of these other
nested and repeated fields.

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:06.910
All right.

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:11.330
So how do you start
selecting these things?

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:11.830
Okey-doke.

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.413
So first off, what I'm going to
do, like, just a simple where.

00:13:14.413 --> 00:13:16.230
We're going to select
round completed.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:27.176
OK, so down here on the query
window, let's see I have to--

00:13:27.176 --> 00:13:29.880
for some reason it's not
